-- title:
--   Normality and branch valuation rings of a node-ring layer
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$. Let $C'\subseteq L$ be a subring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with an element $\varpi'$, such that $C'\subseteq A$, such that an element $d\in C'$ has residue $0$ in the residue field of $A$ exactly when $d\in\varpi'C'$, such that $\varpi'$ is irreducible, and such that every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'$. Let $N_0\subseteq F$ be a Noetherian local subring with $\mathrm{ringKrullDim}\,N_0\ge 2$ containing the image of $C'$, such that for every $g\in N_0$ there is $o\in C'$ whose image lies in $N_0$ with $g-o$ not a unit, and such that for every $n$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to L$ linearly independent over $C'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to N_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ in $F$, all $a_i$ vanish. Let $W_c$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible element $\pi_W$, let $E\ge 1$, let $\sigma:W_c\to \widehat{N_0}$ be a ring homomorphism into the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $N_0$, and let $\iota_c$ be a ring isomorphism of $\widehat{N_0}$ with `UVCrossingModel` $W_c\,(\pi_W^E)$, that is with $W_c[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi_W^E)$, such that: if the image of $\varpi'$ lies in $N_0$ then $\sigma(\pi_W)$ is the canonical image of that element; $\iota_c(\sigma(o))$ is the class of the constant power series $o$ for every $o\in W_c$; and for every $c\in C'$ whose image lies in $N_0$, that image is in the range of $\sigma$. Let $T$ be the subring of $F$ generated by $N_0$ together with the image of $A$, assume every $f\in F$ satisfies $fc=b$ for some $b,c\in T$ with $c\neq 0$, and let $\mathfrak p\subseteq T$ be the ideal spanned by the elements of $T$ equal to a non-unit of $N_0$ together with those equal to the image of an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $L_x\subseteq F$ be a subring whose elements are exactly the $f\in F$ with $fc=b$ for some $b,c\in T$, $c\notin\mathfrak p$. Then: every $f\in F$ integral over $L_x$ lies in $L_x$; and for every prime ideal $Q$ of $L_x$ which contains the image of every element of the maximal ideal of $A$ that lies in $L_x$, and for which some $g\in L_x$ is neither in $Q$ nor a unit, there is a valuation subring $W$ of $F$ consisting exactly of the $f\in F$ with $fc=b$ for some $b,c\in L_x$, $c\notin Q$.
--
--   This provides the two ring-theoretic properties of the localised ring $L_x$ built from a node ring $N_0$ over a discrete layer of constants inside a rank-one valuation ring: $L_x$ is integrally closed in $F$, and its localisation at each branch prime (a prime containing the constants' maximal ideal but not the whole maximal ideal) is a valuation ring of $F$. It is used in the identification of the local ring of a semistable model at an ordinary double point, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_localRing_node_iff_exists_mul_eq_of_nodeChart_of_forall_not_dominates`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.mem_localRing_node_iff_exists_mul_eq_of_nodeChart_of_forall_not_dominates).
